# evidence-timeout: 300
#
# D-129 -- ONE STRAY NON-UTF-8 BYTE IN directives.md SILENTLY VOIDED A LIVE
# URGENT DIRECTIVE, AND Foundry-Clear THEN REPORTED SUCCESS, TRUNCATED THE
# FILE, AND WROTE NO ARCHIVE RECORD. Destroyed data, reported as success.
#
# D-098 had fixed the RAISE -- `_read_text` is tolerant, so an undecodable
# directives.md stopped throwing UnicodeDecodeError out of Foundry-Next -- and
# added NO GUARD HALF. The file was simply read as EMPTY. It was never checked
# because `_run_artifact_problems` globbed `*.json` and nothing else, so the
# one run artifact that is not JSON was the one artifact the guard could not
# see. That is the escalated class exactly: membership derived over the files
# of a TYPE, with the type itself typed.
#
# THE FIX IS NOT "ALSO CHECK directives.md". Naming that file in the guard is
# the same defect one turn later, and the next non-JSON artifact repeats it.
# Membership is derived by globbing every top-level file in the run directory;
# a per-suffix DECODER TABLE says how to read each type. The table is what a
# new artifact TYPE requires -- not a new artifact, which is covered the day it
# is written. spec.md in the table below is the proof: nobody added it, and it
# is guarded.
#
# THE SECOND HALF, and why the decoder alone is not enough. The harm --
# "reports success, truncates, no record" -- is reachable with no encoding
# fault at all: hand-edit a `###` to a `##` and the parser sees no header,
# returns no directives, and the pre-fix clearer truncated a file full of live
# human steering. So the destructive write carries its own conservation check:
# Foundry-Clear may only destroy what it could account for. FR-019 makes
# preserving a record this tool's whole contract, and a truncate that outruns
# the archive breaks it in silence.
#
# The control arm is in the log deliberately: the refusal must be NARROW. A
# readable directive still clears with count 1 and still writes
# directives-cleared.md, and every *.json member was already NAMED before this
# change and still is (NFR-002 -- the fix widens, it narrows nothing).
